<%# The one control that opens the post as someone else would see it, labelled for what
    that actually is: on a draft or a scheduled post the only reader is the writer himself,
    signed in; once it's live there's a real page to send him to. Shared by the post editor
    bar and the HTML-page editor's header, which differ only in button size. Both hrefs
    carry the slug, and both are re-rendered from here when a save renames the post.

    Preview opens in its own tab: the editor stays where the writer left it, and a reload
    of the preview is the whole "refresh" story — no save to lose, no Back to find. %>
<% if post.published? %>
  <%= link_to "View live", public_post_path(post), class: "w-btn w-btn--ghost #{size}" %>
<% else %>
  <%= link_to "Preview", [ :writing, post ], class: "w-btn w-btn--ghost #{size}", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener",
        title: "Only you can see this — it needs your sign-in" %>
<% end %>
